    <h2>Level 80 walkthrough: every move in order<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Steps 1–3</span>
      <strong>Tap the coach’s head (then 2 more)</strong>
      <p>Tap the coach’s head. Swipe right on the head of the player on the left. Tap the referee's money-counting hand.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Steps 4–6</span>
      <strong>Swipe left (then 2 more)</strong>
      <p>Swipe left on the face of the player on the right. Drag the chocolate from the ad to the trophy. Tap the big screen.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Steps 7–9</span>
      <strong>Tap the censored middle finger of the player (then 2 more)</strong>
      <p>Tap the censored middle finger of the player on the right. Drag the paint to the banner. Drag the gold medal from the coach's neck to the middle player.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>If your level 80 shows “Let Her Out”<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>Brain Puzzle 3 does not hand every player the same scene at the same number: builds and
    install order differ, and both variants are on record. If the banner on your screen reads
    “You Can Switch Perspectives With The Button In The Upper Right Corner”, this is that scene, 15 moves in order:</p>
    <ol class="alt-steps">
        <li>Drag The Key To The Door.</li>
        <li>Swipe Left On The Rear Restroom Door.</li>
        <li>Drag The Pliers To The Door.</li>
        <li>Swipe Right On The Wardrobe From The Girl With Glasses' View.</li>
        <li>Drag The Horn To The Door.</li>
        <li>Drag The Cake To The Cat From The Red-haired Girl's View.</li>
        <li>Drag The Cat To The Door.</li>
        <li>Drag The Phone To The Red-haired Girl From The Girl With Glasses' View.</li>
        <li>Drag The Lightning In The Girl's Eyes To The Door.</li>
        <li>Tap The Backpack From The Girl With Glasses' View.</li>
        <li>Drag The Puzzle Piece To The Red-haired Girl.</li>
